  <section id="what-is" aria-labelledby="what-is-h">
    <h2 id="what-is-h">What Is Body Fat Percentage?</h2>
    <p>Body fat percentage is the share of your total body weight that is fat. If you weigh 180&nbsp;lb and carry 36&nbsp;lb of fat, your body fat percentage is 20%. Everything else (muscle, bone, water and organs) is your <strong>lean mass</strong>.</p>
    <p>A <strong>body fat percentage chart</strong> sorts those numbers into bands such as athletic, fit, average and obese. Men and women need different charts because women carry more <em>essential fat</em>, the fat the body needs for hormones and reproduction. That is why 15% is lean for a woman but only fit for a man.</p>
    <p>Two people at the same weight can look very different. Body fat percentage, unlike BMI, tells you how much of that weight is fat and how much is muscle.</p>
  </section>

